00:00:03.429 --> 00:00:04.870 align:start position:0%
as of april 30th donald trump no longer  owns the lease to the trump  international hotel in washington dc  opened in 2016 the hotel's lease  reportedly sold for 370 million dollars  trump and his family will make an  estimated 100 million dollars from the  deal  that's much higher than the 173 million  dollars forbes estimated the hotel to be  worth in october 2021.  we don't know the full picture of how  successful the hotel has been but  because trump was present there is some  public information on the hotel from  when he was in office  trump reported 137 million dollars in  revenue for the hotel during his  presidency during the first three years  the hotel made between 40.4 and 40.8  million dollars in revenue but after  that the business started declining even  before covet restrictions kneecapped  several of the hotel's revenue streams  by his fourth year in office revenue was  down to 15.1 million dollars  additionally a house oversight committee  analysis found that the hotel lost about  73 million dollars between 2016 and  2020.  despite these numbers the hotel was a  hot spot for representatives of foreign  governments trump cabinet officials and  u.s senators a house oversight committee  report estimates that the hotel made  3.75 million dollars in revenue from  foreign governments during the first  three years of trump's presidency the  trump organization for its part says it  only made 459  320 from foreign officials at all of its  hotels resorts and clubs during trump's  presidency that number has not been  independently audited  in all we were able to identify 33  representatives of foreign governments  including malaysia's former president  najib razak and romania's president  klaus johannes 35 of the 65 republicans  who served in the senate while donald  trump was president either visited the  hotel or had a campaign that spent money  there  only one democratic senator visited the  hotel during trump's presidency joe  manchin  and through the federal election  commission forbes found that 3.21  million dollars in campaign spending  took place at the hotel since trump took  office in 2016. this includes 845 000  from the republican national committee  and 566 thousand dollars from america  first action inc a pro-trump super pac  [Music]  you
 

